; SETSPEED: pauses this many seconds after every turtle-motion command
; (FD/BK/RT/LT/SETXY/SETX/SETY/SETHEADING/HOME/ARC), so a drawing
; unfolds step by step instead of snapping straight to the finished
; shape -- for effect, or for watching exactly what a script does one
; move at a time. SPEED reads the current setting back. 0 (the default)
; is instant, same as before SETSPEED existed.

PRINT SPEED   ; 0 -- nothing set yet

SETSPEED 0.15
REPEAT 4 [FD 100 RT 90]   ; each side and turn now takes 0.15s to appear

SETSPEED 0   ; back to instant
REPEAT 4 [FD 60 RT 90]    ; this square snaps straight to finished
